      "writtenOn": "2017-08-17T17:44:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t find code running ectool for \u0027echash ro/rw\u0027. So, I think we can change the meaning of these options.\n\nI\u0027m open to suggestions but here are what I think:\nro: entire RO region\nrw: entire active RW region\n\nIf we ever need to make ectool calculate the hash of an image, instead of adding ro_used or rw_used, we should add a new command \u0027ectool flash_region_info \u003cregion\u003e\u0027, which returns offset and size of a specified region. Then a user should run \u0027ectool echash \u003coffset\u003e \u003csize\u003e\u0027.\n\nIf we ever need to make ectool calculate a specific rw image, we can add:\nrw_a, rw_b, rw_update, rw_active.",
